# .privacy-email-allowlist — known-safe email addresses/domains that are NOT third-party PII.
# Used by scripts/audit-privacy.sh (P936). An email in an ADDED diff line that matches NO
# entry here is flagged as a possible third-party PII leak.
#
# Scope: the email check runs on DIFF CONTENT ONLY — commit messages are never email-scanned
# (they carry Co-Authored-By: <noreply@...> trailers). Existing emails in untouched files are
# not re-scanned (the scanner only sees added/modified lines), so this list need only cover
# addresses/domains that legitimately recur in NEW commits — not every address in the tree.
#
# Grammar (one entry per line; case-insensitive; '#' = comment; blank lines ignored):
#   example.com          bare domain          -> any address @example.com
#   *.example.com        domain-suffix        -> any address whose domain ends .example.com
#   noreply@*            local-part wildcard   -> any address with local part 'noreply'
#   jack@greensock.com   full address          -> that exact address only
#
# To add a safe address: append the NARROWEST entry that covers it. Prefer @example.com for
# NEW test fixtures over allowlisting a real domain. A real third-party person's address does
# NOT belong here — anonymize it instead (.claude/rules/features.md, "PII in Specs").

# --- RFC-reserved / placeholder test domains ---
example.com
*.example.com
example-test.com
example.invalid
example.co.uk
*.example.co.uk
test.com
test.example
email.com
yourdomain.com
domain.tld
bar.com
company.com
mail.company.com

